    "caption": "“Spook Organa” Returns to Charlottetown!\nThis tradition of scary Hallowe’en music will be celebrated at St. Peter’s Cathedral on Sunday October 25 at 7 pm, when members from the Royal Canadian College of Organists presents Spook Organa!, an evening of spooky organ music for all ages. Between the musical selections, creepy tales will be told guaranteed to make the hair stand on end.\nSt. Peter’s is located on All Soul’s Lane in Charlottetown. The one-hour program starts at 7 pm. Admission is by donation. Children 12 and under are asked to bring along a canned good for the food bank. Those who arrive in costume will receive a complimentary treat bag.",
